OVERVIEW: Calculate statistics within a region of interest

USAGE: dicom-measure roi <file-path> [--output <output>] [--format <format>] [--unit <unit>] [--force] [--verbose] [--rect <rect>] [--polygon <polygon> ...] [--circle <circle>] [--statistics] [--histogram] [--bins <bins>]

ARGUMENTS:
  <file-path>             Path to the DICOM file

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <output>   Output file path (prints to stdout if omitted)
  -f, --format <format>   Output format: text, json, csv (values: text, json,
                          csv; default: text)
  --unit <unit>           Unit for measurements: mm, cm, um, inches, pixels
                          (physical units need a pixel spacing; see the
                          overview) (values: mm, cm, um, inches, pixels;
                          default: mm)
  --force                 Force parsing of files without DICM prefix
  --verbose               Verbose output for debugging
  --rect <rect>           Rectangular ROI as x,y,width,height (e.g.,
                          100,100,50,50)
  --polygon <polygon>     Polygon ROI vertices as x,y pairs
  --circle <circle>       Circular ROI as cx,cy,radius (e.g., 200,200,25)
  --statistics            Calculate extended statistics (mean, std, min, max)
  --histogram             Generate pixel value histogram
  --bins <bins>           Number of histogram bins (default: 256)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

